ISSUE:

Description
The normal submission workflow requires the submitter to select an existing canonical fixture.

There is currently no user-facing workflow for an approved submitter to submit event data for a genuinely new fixture that does not yet exist in the platform.

The batch review workflow introduced under #483 can create a canonical fixture from a valid package v1.1 fixture proposal, but the ordinary submitter workflow does not expose a way to originate such a proposal.

As a result, a submitter attempting to capture a new match must rely on the fixture already having been created elsewhere.

Expected behaviour
An approved submitter should be able to submit event data for a new fixture without requiring a manual database insert.

The submission workflow should allow the submitter to either:

select an existing fixture; or
choose New fixture and provide the required fixture metadata.
For a new fixture, the frontend should submit the fixture as a version 1.1 fixture proposal and allow the existing #483 reviewer workflow to create the canonical fixture during review.

The submitter should not directly create canonical fixture data if reviewer approval is required.

Acceptance criteria
The single-fixture submission UI offers a New fixture option.
An approved submitter can provide the required metadata for the new fixture.
The generated submission uses the existing version 1.1 fixture-proposal contract.
The new fixture does not require direct database editing.
The submission can progress to reviewer resolution.
An administrator can use the existing Create canonical fixture from proposal action.
After canonical fixture creation, the affected submission is revalidated/resolved.
Existing-fixture submissions continue to work unchanged.
Automated tests cover both existing-fixture and new-fixture submission paths.
Relationship to #483
#483 implemented the administrator-side canonical fixture creation decision.

This issue completes the submitter-side workflow required to actually originate a genuinely new fixture through the application.

